#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# generalized_momenta

#% text
# `generalized_momenta(L, q, t)` gives the canonical momenta `dL/dq'` of the coordinates `q` (a function `x(t)`, its name, or a list) of the Lagrangian `L`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The result is a list with one momentum per coordinate.

#% item
# The momentum of a coordinate that does not occur in `L` itself (a cyclic coordinate) is conserved.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
generalized_momenta(m*x'(t)^2/2 - k*x(t)^2/2, x, t)
#% output
#= [m*x'(t)]

#% cell
generalized_momenta(m*(r'(t)^2 + r(t)^2*th'(t)^2)/2 - V(r(t)), [r, th], t)
#% output
#= [m*r'(t), m*r(t)^2*th'(t)]

#% text
# The momentum of a charge differs from `m x'` by the vector potential:

#% cell
generalized_momenta(m*x'(t)^2/2 + e0*x'(t)*A(x(t)), x, t)
#% output
#= [e0*A(x(t)) + m*x'(t)]

